stale_hash.py (the two designs)<pre><code>@dataclass
class IdentityConfig:
    """Static configuration hashed by object identity: the compile cache cannot see a mutated field."""

    n_worst: int

    def __hash__(self) -&gt; int:
        """Identity, like ToOp's SolverConfig.__hash__."""
        return id(self)

    def __eq__(self, other: object) -&gt; bool:
        """Identity, like ToOp's SolverConfig.__eq__."""
        return self is other


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class FrozenConfig:
    """Static configuration hashed by value: a new value is a new cache key, an equal value hits the cache."""

    n_worst: int
</code></pre> <p>Open the <code>src/</code> folder on GitHub to see or download all the files of this chapter.</p> <p><code>worst = jax.jit(_worst, static_argnums=1)</code> returns the <code>config.n_worst</code> largest |flows|. With <code>IdentityConfig(n_worst=3)</code> the result has shape <code>(3,)</code>; after <code>config.n_worst = 5</code> in place it is still <code>(3,)</code>, the stale program, and the Python counter inside <code>_worst</code> confirms that the second call did not trace; <code>worst(flows, replace(config, n_worst=5))</code> traces again and returns <code>(5,)</code>. With <code>FrozenConfig</code>, 3 → <code>(3,)</code>, 5 → <code>(5,)</code>, and a third call with a new <code>FrozenConfig(3)</code> is a cache hit: two traces in total. The test that would have caught the trap is the check that a result follows the configuration it was computed with, <code>assert worst(flows, config).shape == (config.n_worst,)</code> after the mutation: <code>test_stale_hash.py</code> shows it failing for <code>IdentityConfig</code> (wrapped in <code>pytest.raises(AssertionError)</code>, so the suite stays green) and passing for <code>FrozenConfig</code>. In ToOp's own suite, <code>test_jax_compilation.py</code> guards the other direction (no spurious retrace) with <code>jax.no_tracing()</code>; a test of this direction (a changed static field must change the output) is what was missing.</p>
